#
# DEVS:Internet/service_discovery
#
# Servers running on this Amiga, announced to the rest of the network so that
# a Mac, a Linux box or Windows finds them without being told an address.
#
# THIS IS NOT DEVS:Internet/services.  That file is the /etc/services table:
# it says which port number the name "ftp" means, for every machine.  This
# one says which servers are running HERE, and nothing else reads it.
#
# NOTHING IS ANNOUNCED UNLESS YOU PUT IT HERE.  AmiNetXDuo ships clients and
# no servers, so it has nothing of its own to advertise.  What it can
# advertise is a server you installed -- AmiFTPd, a web server, a file server
# -- because you are the one who knows it is running.  Announcing a port with
# nothing behind it is worse than announcing nothing: the other machine will
# list it, connect, and hang.
#
# One line per service:
#
#     <type>  <port>  [name]  [txt=key=value;key=value]
#
#   type    what kind of server it is, in the standard form: an underscore,
#           up to fifteen letters, digits or hyphens, then ._tcp or ._udp.
#   port    the port it is really listening on, 1 to 65535.
#   name    what it is called in the other machine's list.  It may contain
#           spaces and runs to the end of the line.  Leave it out and this
#           Amiga's host name is used, which is usually what you want.
#   txt=    extra settings some clients look for, separated by ';'.
#           Optional.
#
# '#' starts a comment anywhere on a line.  A ';' at the start of a line is a
# comment too, but not one in the middle: ';' separates txt= settings.
#
# A line with a mistake in it is reported and skipped.  The rest of the file,
# and the network, come up as usual.
#

# An FTP server on the usual port, listed under this Amiga's own name:
#
#_ftp._tcp     21

# A web server, with a name of its own and the path browsers should open:
#
#_http._tcp    80    Amiga web server    txt=path=/

# Some other things you might be running.  Use the port your server is
# actually configured for, not the one written here.
#
#_telnet._tcp  23
#_ssh._tcp     22
#_smb._tcp     139   Amiga file share
#_afpovertcp._tcp 548
#_daap._tcp    3689  Amiga music

# At most eight services are announced.
